'''Destiny Usman Garuba Alari''' (born 9 March 2002) is a Spanish professional [[basketball]] player for [[Real Madrid Baloncesto|Real Madrid]] of the Spanish [[Liga ACB]] and the [[EuroLeague]]. Listed at {{height|m=2.03}}, he plays at both the [[power forward]] and [[center (basketball)|center]] positions.

Garuba was born in [[Madrid]], Spain to Nigerian parents and joined the youth academy of Real Madrid at age 11. In 2019, when he was 17 years old, he became the youngest starter in Real Madrid history. In the 2020–21 season, Garuba was named [[EuroLeague Rising Star]] and [[ACB Best Young Player Award|ACB Best Young Player]]. He earned [[most valuable player]] (MVP) honors at the [[2016 FIBA U16 European Championship]] at age 14. In the [[2021 NBA draft]], he was selected by the [[Houston Rockets]] with the 23rd overall pick.
